Subject: [PATCH 5/5] sr-aef: name glyphs as a feature file can

A post table can name a glyph with characters a feature file cannot hold:
GFS Neohellenic has "Numero sign", which the uncompiled GDEF class read as two
glyphs, "Numero" and "sign", and fontc refused the features. A character
outside A-Z a-z 0-9 . _ - now becomes _, and a name starting with a digit or a
hyphen gets a leading _. Kirang Haerang names thousands of glyphs ".notdef",
which were made unique as ".notdef.487" and the like, names a feature file
refuses (it takes a leading period only in .notdef): a repeated name starting
with a period now becomes "_notdef.1" and so on. A name the font gives once,
such as ".ttfautohint", is kept.

Assisted by an AI agent (Claude Opus 5.5)
